{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Nethanel son of Zuar presented … present his offering.</b> Why does Scripture say הִקְרִיב regarding the tribe of Issachar, which it did not say regarding all the tribes? Because Reuben came and objected and said: Since Judah preceded me, I will present after him. Moses said to him: From the mouth of the Gevurah it was told to me that they shall present in the order of the encampments — by their standards. Therefore it says הַקְרֵב אֶת קָרְבָּנוֹ, and it is missing a yod, so that it conveys הַקְרֵב — an expression of command, for from the mouth of the Gevurah he was commanded הַקְרֵב. And what is הִקְרִיב הִקְרִיב, twice? Because for two things he merited to present second among the tribes: one, that they were knowledgeable in Torah, as it says ״וּמִבְּנֵי יִשָּׂשכָר יוֹדְעֵי בִינָה לַעִתִּים״ (I Chronicles 12), and one, that they gave counsel to the princes to donate these offerings. And in the foundation of Rabbi Moshe ha-Darshan I found: Rabbi Pinchas ben Yair said — Nethanel ben Zuar suggested this counsel to them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:51.999750081Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}